 ### Teardown Hierarchical Traversal
-A hierarchical traversal method that uses DDA within a level and switches levels by rescaling the grid so the new level becomes a level 0 grid, restarting the DDA algorithm [S13, unofficial]. It calculates ray position using $pos = \lfloor (O + t \cdot D) / 2^{level} \rfloor$. Pitfalls include floating-point issues causing outliers in depth/normal buffers and rays traversing corners causing normal issues [S13, unofficial].
